  500:     "and it tracks the datum, so the predicate saw it")
  501: 
  502: #  R4 -- the LATCH at site B.
  503: A = Addr(CODE)
  504: t, alive, how = session(store16(GDROM_COND, 0x0055, A)
  505:                         + store16(GDROM_COND, 0x0056, A)
  506:                         + store16(GDROM_COND, 0x0057, A))
  507: row("R4 cond x3", "%d" % len(COND_RE.findall(t)), "1",
  508:     "three bad writes at B, ONE diagnostic")
  509: 
  510: # ------------------------------------------------------------------ R5  *** THE KEYSTONE
  511: #  *** ANCHORED, AND THE ANCHOR IS THE WHOLE POINT (clause f). ***
  512: #  A fresh device has cond == 0.  So the naive row -- "write 0x55, read back 0" -- is
  513: #  satisfied by the CORRECT fix and ALSO by a mutant that assigns d->cond = 0 on decline.
  514: #  Driving an ACCEPTED 0xef FIRST puts a value in cond that only the accept arm can have
  515: #  placed there; requiring 0xef back after the declined write separates the two.
  516: #
  517: #  This is the row that kills the clause-(d) mutant BOTH Agent seats named independently on
  518: #  pass 1: keep the latched decline, move `d->cond = idata;` back above the dispatch.  Under
  519: #  that mutant this reads 0x55.  Every other row in this file stays green.
  520: A = Addr(CODE)
  521: t, alive, how = session(store16(GDROM_COND, 0x00ef, A)
  522:                         + store16(GDROM_COND, 0x0055, A)
  523:                         + load16(GDROM_COND, A))
  524: row("R5 cond keep", printed(t, "r2"), "0xef",
  525:     "*** ANCHORED: declined write leaves d->cond UNCHANGED")
  526: 
  527: #  *** ONE ANCHOR IS NOT ENOUGH, AND A SEAT MEASURED WHY ON PASS 2. ***
  528: #  R5 alone pins "cond == 0xef after the sequence", which the CORRECT fix satisfies and so
  529: #  does a one-line mutant `d->cond = 0xef;` in the decline arm.  That mutant fabricates
  530: #  COND_DATA_AVAIL (0xef & 0x08) out of a fresh or 0xa0-anchored decline and unlocks the
  531: #  GDROM_DATA read path -- the exact defect R5 exists to prevent, walking straight past it.
  532: #
  533: #  THE REPAIR IS PRE-STATES, NOT MORE ROWS OF THE SAME SHAPE.  "Unchanged" is a claim about
  534: #  a FUNCTION of the prior value, and one sample cannot distinguish a function from a
  535: #  constant.  Three samples over the model's principal reachable states pin it: any
  536: #  constant, any zeroing, any OR, and idata itself all differ from the identity on at least
  537: #  one of them.
  538: #  *** THE DECLINED BYTE HERE IS 0xaa, NOT 0x55, AND THE CHANGE IS ONE CONSTANT THAT CLOSES
  539: #  A MEASURED ESCAPE. ***  With 0x55 the three declined values were {0x55, 0x55, 0x08},
  540: #  whose union is 0x5d -- so BITS 1, 5 AND 7 APPEARED IN NO PROBED VALUE, and R5/R5b/R5c
  541: #  were blind to any VALUE-CONDITIONAL store keyed on them.  The opus5 seat built one and
  542: #  measured all 20 rows identical to the fix tree:
  543: #
  544: #      +		if (idata >= 0x80)
  545: #      +			d->cond = idata;
  546: #
  547: #  Its plausible dress writes itself -- "0xa0 and 0xef are both >= 0x80, so high bytes are
  548: #  command codes; let them land" -- and a declined 0x88 then stores 0x88, whose bit 3 FORGES
  549: #  COND_DATA_AVAIL: the exact defect the store relocation exists to prevent.
  550: #
  551: #  {0x55, 0xaa, 0x08} spans all eight bits, so no conditional keyed on any single bit can
  552: #  pass all three.  The three rows now test the map on a spanning set rather than on an
  553: #  arbitrary one.  *Zero new rows; the cost of the original hole was that nobody asked which
  554: #  bits the probed values covered.*
  555: A = Addr(CODE)
  556: t, alive, how = session(store16(GDROM_COND, 0x00aa, A) + load16(GDROM_COND, A))
  557: row("R5b cond 00", printed(t, "r2"), "0x0",
  558:     "FRESH pre-state: decline leaves cond at its reset 0")
  559: 
  560: A = Addr(CODE)
  561: #  the declined byte here is 0x08 -- COND_DATA_AVAIL itself -- so the row MEASURES the
  562: #  forge subspace instead of inferring it: any mutant that stores or ORs the declined
  563: #  value lands data-available on top of an accepted 0xa0, and this reds.
  564: t, alive, how = session(store16(GDROM_COND, 0x00a0, A)
  565:                         + store16(GDROM_COND, 0x0008, A)
  566:                         + load16(GDROM_COND, A))
  567: row("R5c cond a0", printed(t, "r2"), "0xa0",
  568:     "0xa0 pre-state: decline preserves the ACCEPTED value")
  569: 
  570: #  *** SPANNING THE BITS KILLS SINGLE-BIT PREDICATES AND NOT CONJUNCTIONS.  Named by the
  571: #  codex seat AFTER the spanning repair had already landed -- which is the useful shape of a
  572: #  finding: accept the repair, then ask what it does NOT buy. ***
  573: #
  574: #  The three declined bytes {0x55, 0xaa, 0x08} union to 0xff, so no SINGLE-bit conditional
  575: #  can pass all three.  A CONJUNCTION can:
  576: #
  577: #      if ((idata & 0x09) == 0x09)
  578: #              d->cond = idata;
  579: #
  580: #  0x55 carries bit 0 and not bit 3; 0xaa and 0x08 carry bit 3 and not bit 0.  **NOT ONE OF
  581: #  THE THREE HAS BOTH**, so every existing row stays green while a declined 0x09 stores 0x09
  582: #  and forges COND_DATA_AVAIL.  0x09 is the smallest value carrying the readiness bit
  583: #  together with a bit no other probed value pairs it with.
  584: #
  585: #  HONEST BOUND, because a spanning argument invites exactly this overclaim: this closes
  586: #  two-bit conjunctions involving bit 3.  It does not close the general k-bit case, and the
  587: #  contract covers every unmodelled value while four samples do not.  Stated rather than
  588: #  implied.
  589: A = Addr(CODE)
  590: t, alive, how = session(store16(GDROM_COND, 0x00ef, A)
  591:                         + store16(GDROM_COND, 0x0009, A)
  592:                         + load16(GDROM_COND, A))
  593: #  THE 09 ANNOUNCEMENT IS IN THE ORACLE because without it this row is store-death-unsafe:
  594: #  if the 0x09 store is missed while the ANCHOR and the LOAD both run, the read still
  595: #  returns 0xef and the row passes having observed nothing.  Named by a seat as an eighth
  596: #  `storesidedead` member -- the class applies to a row that drives TWO stores whenever
  597: #  only one of them is load-bearing.
  598: m = COND_RE.search(t)
  599: #  *** AND THE MUTANT THIS ROW USED TO NAME IS ONE R12b ALREADY SUBSUMES.  Corrected
  600: #  2026-08-30 by the adjudicating seat, which checked rather than agreed. ***
  601: #
  602: #  The stated mutant was a conjunction `(idata & 0x09) == 0x09`.  R12b drives 0xff, and
  603: #  0xff passes EVERY `(idata & M) == M` -- so R12b kills that form on its own and this
  604: #  row adds nothing against it.  A row is justified by a mutant no OTHER row catches,
  605: #  and citing a subsumed one overstates the suite while looking like coverage.
  606: #
  607: #  THE DISCRIMINATING FORM IS AN EXACT LOW-NIBBLE MATCH, `(idata & 0x0f) == 0x09`:
  608: #      0xff -> 0x0f != 0x09   R12b stays GREEN and misses it
  609: #      0x09 -> forges cond=0x09, and this row reds on field 1 (0x9 != 0xef)
  610: #  So R5d earns its place -- on that mutant, not on the one it used to claim.
  611: #
  612: #  LATENT FRAGILITY, worth stating because it is invisible from the row: field 2 works
  613: #  ONLY while 0xef stays an ACCEPTED value.  The device announces nothing for 0xef, so
  614: #  the sole COND_RE match is the 0x09 decline.  If a future round moved 0xef to the
  615: #  declined side, field 2 STOPS OBSERVING THE 0x09 DECLINE and starts observing
  616: #  whatever the anchor's own decline printed instead.  The row reds -- loudly, which is
  617: #  the safe direction -- but for a reason unrelated to the rule under test, so whoever
  618: #  sees it should read this note before re-pinning.
  619: #
  620: #  *** AN EARLIER DRAFT OF THIS NOTE PREDICTED THE OBSERVABLE AND GOT IT WRONG, WHICH
  621: #  IS WHY IT NO LONGER PREDICTS ONE. ***  It said field 2 would read "absent".  It
  622: #  would not: the anchor's decline goes through the SAME else arm and prints
  623: #  `unimplemented GDROM_COND = 0xef ... (once)`, and COND_RE.search returns the FIRST
  624: #  match -- so field 2 reads "ef".  (And if a future decline used different text, the
  625: #  0x09 latch would be unconsumed and field 2 would read "09" with field 1 red
  626: #  instead.)  Caught by the adjudicating seat.  The DIRECTION was right and the
  627: #  mechanism was wrong -- which is `read the line before citing it`, inside a
